{
  "spec": "paladin-holy",
  "state": "written",
  "notes": "Written for the fork's healing sim (sim/healsim: the healer is raid player 0, players 1-4 its party, player 5 the tank). Flash of Light is the staple, Holy Light covers a tank below 40 percent behind Divine Favor, and the instant Holy Shock and a second Holy Light line spend mana only while it is no further behind the fight clock than five points (currentManaPercent against remainingTimePercent). The paced lines open when the mana bar is no further behind the fight clock than five points: a healer with spare mana reaches them often, and a healer short of mana only now and then (Holy Shock at a fixed threshold, with no pacing, healed less than the paced line). Light's Vigil (a party heal through the next Holy Shock on its target, 1340 mana at level 60) is in the engine but left out of this rotation: it lowered effective HPS by 2 to 9 percent in every variant tried, because the profile's raid pulses (300 damage on three members) are too small for a five-target heal that costs as much mana as almost ten Flash of Lights. Ranks follow one rule, stated in design/reviews/2026-10-08-healer-mana-audit.md: starting from the top ranks, a lower rank (any rank; Forever has no sub-20 cut on heals, so round 22 re-judged the ranks learned below 20 level by level) is taken for a spell when it raises the ranker's guarded score by more than two percent, the biggest gain first, the tank's casts and the party members' casts counted apart, and compared on the raid gear the ranker published for the list being tried. The engine states the client's own numbers for every rank with no downrank penalty, so a lower rank is a statement about this profile, not a measurement of the game. The site runs this list as written at band 60; below 60 each ranked spell casts the highest rank learned that is not above the rank named here, unless data/curated/rank-choices.json names another rank for the band (owner ruling 3, sim-accuracy round 9). Here that is Holy Shock at rank 1, Flash of Light at rank 4 on the four party members and, since round 9 (owner ruling 3, design/reviews/2026-11-02-sim-audit-round9/ranks.md), Flash of Light at rank 1 on the tank; every other spell keeps its top rank. The comparison is repeated on the gear each new list makes the ranker choose until no spell moves. No Blessing of Light before the pull: Forever removed Blessing of Light and Greater Blessing of Light (round 6 pipeline P5, the 70707 hotfix push). Oath of Light, the Holy talent that took its place, is sworn on the tank before the pull instead (round 7, design/reviews/2026-11-02-sim-audit-round7/healers.md); Holy Shock on the sworn tank gives up Boundless Light's crit, which the extra healing outweighs. Spirit regeneration, mp5 and the five second rule are the engine's own formulas (the client publishes no spirit regeneration table). Every healer number comes from the engine's fake raid, not from a boss fight. Round 6 (design/reviews/2026-11-02-sim-audit-round6/healers.md): the heal profile's raid-wide pulses now land on the healer as well, three of the five members of the group a pulse. You are healed like the other four party members.",
  "expected_idle": [
    {
      "id": 1311606,
      "reason": "Holy Shock is a paced line: it opens only while the healer's mana bar is no further behind the fight clock than five points, and the rotation's own notes say a healer short of mana reaches it only now and then. The ladder's bare healer, against the heal profile's pulses, is that healer: measured over 300 iterations it casts Holy Shock zero times at levels 38 to 60, so the paced line is idle on every rung where it is learned."
    }
  ],
